{"id":"5f228216-2b50-47e9-81d3-e13d46a16a5d","object":"chat.completion","created":1784996031,"model":"deepseek-v4-flash","choices":[{"index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"{\n  \"implementation\": \"def solve(case):\\n    # Validate case\\n    if 'nodes' not in case or 'required_symbols' not in case:\\n        raise ValueError(\\\"Missing 'nodes' or 'required_symbols' in case\\\")\\n    nodes = case['nodes']\\n    required_symbols = case['required_symbols']\\n    if not isinstance(nodes, list) or not isinstance(required_symbols, list):\\n        raise ValueError(\\\"Invalid types for nodes or required_symbols\\\")\\n    if len(nodes) == 0:\\n        raise ValueError(\\\"Empty nodes list\\\")\\n    \\n    # Build maps: id->node, id->children\\n    node_map = {}\\n    children_map = {}  # id -> list of child ids\\n    root_id = None\\n    for node in nodes:\\n        nid = node['id']\\n        node_map[nid] = node\\n        parent = node.get('parent')\\n        if parent is None:\\n            if root_id is not None:\\n                raise ValueError(\\\"Multiple roots\\\")\\n            root_id = nid\\n        else:\\n            children_map.setdefault(parent, []).append(nid)\\n    if root_id is None:\\n        raise ValueError(\\\"No root node\\\")\\n    \\n    # Initial symbol counts (all nodes retained)\\n    symbol_counts = {}\\n    for node in node_map.values():\\n        sym = node['symbol']\\n        symbol_counts[sym] = symbol_counts.get(sym, 0) + 1\\n    \\n    # Sort nodes by depth descending, then id ascending for stable ties\\n    sorted_nodes = sorted(node_map.values(), key=lambda n: (-n['depth'], n['id']))\\n    \\n    removed_set = set()\\n    removed_order = []\\n    \\n    # Helper to compute subtree symbol counts for nodes not already removed\\n    def subtree_counts(node_id):\\n        counts = {}\\n        stack = [node_id]\\n        while stack:\\n            nid = stack.pop()\\n            if nid in removed_set:\\n                continue  # already removed, skip\\n            node = node_map[nid]\\n            sym = node['symbol']\\n            counts[sym] = counts.get(sym, 0) + 1\\n            for child in children_map.get(nid, []):\\n                stack.append(child)\\n        return counts\\n    \\n    for node in sorted_nodes:\\n        nid = node['id']\\n        if nid in removed_set:\\n            continue\\n        # Never remove root\\n        if nid == root_id:\\n            continue\\n        # Never remove node with required symbol\\n        if node['symbol'] in required_symbols:\\n            continue\\n        if not node['removable']:\\n            continue\\n        # Check children: any child not removed -> cannot remove parent\\n        child_ids = children_map.get(nid, [])\\n        has_retained_child = any(cid not in removed_set for cid in child_ids)\\n        if has_retained_child:\\n            continue\\n        # Compute subtree counts for nodes still retained (would be removed)\\n        sub_counts = subtree_counts(nid)\\n        # Check if removing these would drop any required symbol to zero\\n        feasible = True\\n        for req in required_symbols:\\n            current = symbol_counts.get(req, 0)\\n            to_remove = sub_counts.get(req, 0)\\n            if current - to_remove < 1:\\n                feasible = False\\n                break\\n        if not feasible:\\n            continue\\n        # Perform removal: add node and all retained descendants to removed_set\\n        # We need to collect all nodes in subtree that are not already removed\\n        to_remove_nodes = []\\n        stack = [nid]\\n        while stack:\\n            cur_id = stack.pop()\\n            if cur_id in removed_set:\\n                continue\\n            to_remove_nodes.append(cur_id)\\n            for child in children_map.get(cur_id, []):\\n                stack.append(child)\\n        for rid in to_remove_nodes:\\n            removed_set.add(rid)\\n            # Update symbol counts\\n            sym = node_map[rid]['symbol']\\n            symbol_counts[sym] -= 1\\n            if symbol_counts[sym] == 0:\\n                del symbol_counts[sym]\\n        # Record removal order (only the top node, as per spec? The problem says 'actual removal order' - likely order of removal decisions, not each node individually. The output schema shows removed_node_ids as array of strings, presumably the ids of nodes that were removed entirely (the ones we decided to remove). But when we remove a parent, its children are also removed but not separately listed. The spec says \\\"Return sorted retained IDs and the actual removal order.\\\" The fixture example? Not given. But likely the removal order is the order in which we remove nodes (parent removals). We'll add only the top node id.\\n        removed_order.append(nid)\\n    \\n    # Retained nodes: all nodes not removed\\n    retained_ids = sorted([nid for nid in node_map if nid not in removed_set])\\n    \\n    return {\\n        'removed_node_ids': removed_order,\\n        'retained_node_ids': retained_ids\\n    }\\n\"\n}","reasoning_content":"We need to implement `solve(case)` that implements a grammar-guided node reduction algorithm. The task is to reduce a parse tree (nodes with id, parent, symbol, depth, removable, utility) while preserving required_symbols. The algorithm should consider deeper nodes before shallower ones, never remove root, required symbols, or nodes with retained children. Tentatively remove a node only if all required symbols remain represented. Use node ID as stable tie break at equal depth. Return sorted retained IDs and actual removal order.\n\nGiven the output schema: removed_node_ids (list of strings, order of removal), retained_node_ids (list of strings, sorted). The case payload has nodes list and required_symbols list.\n\nWe need to simulate the reduction. First, build a tree structure from nodes. Each node has id, parent (null for root), symbol, depth, removable, utility. We need to traverse nodes in order of decreasing depth, and for same depth, tie-break by something? The description says \"Use node ID as the stable tie break at equal depth.\" But for processing order, it says \"Consider deeper parse-tree nodes before shallower nodes.\" So we iterate nodes sorted by depth descending, and for equal depth, presumably by id (string) as stable tie-break.\n\nFor each node, if it is removable, we tentatively check if removing it (and all its descendants) would still preserve all required_symbols. But careful: \"Tentatively remove a node only if all required symbols remain represented.\" That implies we check the set of symbols in the remaining tree after removal. Also \"Never remove the root, a required symbol, or a node with retained children.\" So we also check that node's symbol is not in required_symbols (if a node's symbol is required, it cannot be removed). Also if the node has children that are retained (i.e., not removed), then it cannot be removed because removal would remove its children. But we are processing in order; when we tentatively remove a node, we remove it and its entire subtree. So children are not yet removed? Actually we process deeper nodes first, so children (deeper) are considered before parent. So when we consider a parent, its children might have been already removed. So condition \"node with retained children\" means if any child still present (not removed) then cannot remove parent. Since we process deeper first, children are already considered; but we need to track which nodes are removed. So we need a set of removed nodes initially empty. When we consider a node, we check if it's removable, not root, its symbol not in required_symbols, and if after removing its subtree, all required symbols still exist in the remaining tree (excluding this subtree). Also we need to check if any of its children are retained? Actually if a child is retained (not removed), then removing the parent would also